      "position": 0,
      "content": "THE ARTICULATION AGREEMENT BELOW IS SUBJECT TO PERIODIC REVISION. PLEASE CONSULT A COUNSELOR EVERY SEMESTER TO OBTAIN CURRENT INFORMATION ABOUT POSSIBLE CHANGES IN THE AGREEMENT.",
      "contentHtml": "THE ARTICULATION AGREEMENT BELOW IS SUBJECT TO PERIODIC REVISION. PLEASE CONSULT A COUNSELOR EVERY SEMESTER TO OBTAIN CURRENT INFORMATION ABOUT POSSIBLE CHANGES IN THE AGREEMENT."
    },
    {
      "id": "a7b16845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "This agreement primarily displays only the lower-division courses required in the major, and a few featured upper-division courses. Although completion of the coursework below is not necessarily mandatory prior to admission, students are strongly advised to complete as much lower division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. This agreement does not contain most upper-division (junior-senior) major requirements, course pre-requisites, general education or all-university coursework necessary for completion of this degree. In some cases, there may be alternative course options at the upper-division level. REFER TO THE FRESNO STATE CATALOG FOR FURTHER INFORMATION: http://www.fresnostate.edu/catalog/",
      "contentHtml": "<p>This agreement primarily displays only the lower-division courses required in the major, and a few featured upper-division courses. Although completion of the coursework below is not necessarily mandatory prior to admission, students are strongly advised to complete as much lower division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. This agreement does not contain most upper-division (junior-senior) major requirements, course pre-requisites, general education or all-university coursework necessary for completion of this degree. In some cases, there may be alternative course options at the upper-division level. REFER TO THE FRESNO STATE CATALOG FOR FURTHER INFORMATION: <a href=\"http://www.fresnostate.edu/catalog/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.fresnostate.edu/catalog/</a></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "acb16845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "General Information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "aab16845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Africana Studies emphasizes the study of the history and culture of African Americans as they relate to the experiences of Africans on the continent and other peoples of African descent in the Diaspora. A major in Africana Studies provides an epistemological basis for understanding issues that pertain to the experiences of African peoples and other minority ethnic groups in the American society. The curriculum promotes an awareness of the African heritage of African Americans and others throughout the Americas. Opportunities are provided for students to engage in study abroad and service-learning in Africa and the Caribbean to stimulate intellectual interest in, and linkage to, contemporary Africa and the African Diaspora while enhancing global understanding of the varied social realities of the human experience. Advising Notes: Other Degree Requirements: In addition to the major program requirements, every student must also complete the University’s baccalaureate degree requirements such as: American Government and Institutions ( PLSI 2 ) General Education Requirements (43 units) General Education, Additional University Graduation Requirements, and Upper-division Writing courses can be double counted with major requirements. These courses include AFRS 10 , AFRS 15 , or AFRS 27 (Area 6), AFRS 36 (Area 4B), AFRS 144 (Area UD4), AFRS 150 or AFRS 164 (AUGR M/I). See advisor for details. Additional University Graduation Requirements (9 units) Upper-Division Writing Requirement Sufficient Elective Units to Meet Required Total Units (varies); it is recommended that units in this area be utilized to complete a second major or minor. Double B.A. Major in Africana Studies A double B.A. major in Africana Studies will consist of 33 units, of which 24 units will be in Africana Studies. Fifteen units of the 24 units must be upper division. Units can be double counted. Students are strongly encouraged to see an Africana Studies academic advisor for assistance in planning the major.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Africana Studies emphasizes the study of the history and culture of African Americans as they relate to the experiences of Africans on the continent and other peoples of African descent in the Diaspora. A major in Africana Studies provides an epistemological basis for understanding issues that pertain to the experiences of African peoples and other minority ethnic groups in the American society. The curriculum promotes an awareness of the African heritage of African Americans and others throughout the Americas. Opportunities are provided for students to engage in study abroad and service-learning in Africa and the Caribbean to stimulate intellectual interest in, and linkage to, contemporary Africa and the African Diaspora while enhancing global understanding of the varied social realities of the human experience.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Advising Notes:</strong></p><p><u style=\"background-color: transparent; font-size: 16px;\">Other Degree Requirements:</u></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">In addition to the major program requirements, every student must also complete the University’s baccalaureate degree requirements such as:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">American Government and Institutions (</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3102&amp;returnto=230#tt9532\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">PLSI 2</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">)</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=249\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">General Education</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;Requirements (43&nbsp;units)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">General Education, Additional University Graduation Requirements, and Upper-division Writing courses can be double counted with major requirements. These courses include&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3102&amp;returnto=230#tt5016\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">AFRS 10</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">,&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3102&amp;returnto=230#tt2000\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">AFRS 15</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">, or&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3102&amp;returnto=230#tt631\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">AFRS 27</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;(Area 6),&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3102&amp;returnto=230#tt2372\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">AFRS 36</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;(Area 4B),&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3102&amp;returnto=230#tt4335\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">AFRS 144</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;(Area UD4),&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3102&amp;returnto=230#tt5060\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">AFRS 150</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;or&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3102&amp;returnto=230#tt1135\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">AFRS 164</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;(AUGR M/I).&nbsp;See advisor for details.</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Additional University Graduation Requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;(9 units)&nbsp;</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=245\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Upper-Division Writing</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;Requirement</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Sufficient Elective Units to Meet Required Total Units (varies); it is recommended that units in this area be utilized to complete a second major or minor.</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><u style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Double B.A. Major in Africana Studies</u></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">A double B.A. major in Africana Studies will consist of 33 units, of which 24 units will be in Africana Studies. Fifteen units of the 24 units must be upper division. Units can be double counted. Students are strongly encouraged to see an Africana Studies academic advisor for assistance in planning the major.</span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "639b0a24-a602-44d6-9d2f-01982e92b4a8",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Additional University Graduation Requirements The Additional University Graduation Requirements are designed to complement the GE requirements. It is the policy of Fresno State, that all students will cultivate and refine their affective, cognitive, and physical faculties through studying great works of the human imagination; be equipped for lifelong understanding and development of themselves as integrated physiological, social, and psychological beings; and be prepared to understand and live in a multicultural and international world through their undergraduate education. This will be accomplished through a total of 9 units from the following areas, each requiring 3 units: Arts/Humanities (A/H) - All students are required to take an Arts/Humanities course to graduate at the bachelor’s degree level. Lifelong-Understanding and Self-Development (L/S) - All students are required to take a lifelong understanding and self-development course to for graduate at the bachelor’s degree level. Multicultural/International (M/I) - All Students are required to take a Multicultural / International course at Fresno State to graduate at the bachelor’s degree level.",
      "contentHtml": "<h1>Additional University Graduation Requirements</h1><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The&nbsp;Additional University Graduation Requirements are designed to complement the GE requirements. It is the policy of Fresno State, that all students will cultivate and refine their affective, cognitive, and physical faculties through studying great works of the human imagination; be equipped for lifelong understanding and development of themselves as integrated physiological, social, and psychological beings; and be prepared to understand and live in a multicultural and international world through their undergraduate education.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This will be accomplished through a total of 9 units from the following areas, each requiring 3 units:</span></p><ol><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279#ah\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Arts/Humanities (A/H)</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;All students are required to take an Arts/Humanities&nbsp;course to graduate&nbsp;at the bachelor’s degree level.&nbsp;</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279#ls\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Lifelong-Understanding and Self-Development (L/S)</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;All students are required to take a lifelong understanding and self-development course to&nbsp;for graduate&nbsp;at the bachelor’s degree level.&nbsp;</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279#mi\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Multicultural/International (M/I)</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;All Students are required to take a Multicultural / International course at Fresno State to graduate&nbsp;at the bachelor’s degree level.&nbsp;</span></li></ol>"
    }
  ],
